  "global_spatial_rules": [
    "Do not force every region into a similar rectangular footprint; extent and room density follow local identity.",
    "Build at least three distinct vertical strata: upper forest/monastery, central settlement/city, and lower reservoir/tomb/relic layers.",
    "Every hub should have visually distinct exits whose spatial positions communicate direction and elevation.",
    "Every major shortcut must change actual traversal cost or route options after activation.",
    "Locked vistas should be visible from a reachable viewpoint before the route is opened.",
    "Optional hidden regions H01-H08 must not block ordinary completion; discoveries may alter ending conditions.",
    "Use room clusters, vertical connectors and multi-region loops instead of one long corridor or a chain of isolated test rooms.",
    "Mainline and shortcut graph must be validated against real collision, jump reach, death recovery and save/load."
  ],
